1
00:00:00,629 --> 00:00:06,641
(A Bona fide Killer)

2
00:00:08,659 --> 00:00:10,494
(This drama, its characters,
and events are fictional.)

3
00:00:10,494 --> 00:00:11,643
(Scenes with child actors
and animals were supervised.)

4
00:00:11,737 --> 00:00:13,672
(Episode 3)

5
00:00:16,253 --> 00:00:17,488
- Hello.
- Hi.

6
00:00:28,899 --> 00:00:30,434
You're going to stare a hole through it.

7
00:00:30,901 --> 00:00:32,736
This isn't a test, so take it easy.

8
00:00:32,903 --> 00:00:35,439
This is going to be a long one,
so brace yourself. Go home.

9
00:00:35,439 --> 00:00:36,640
Sir, take a look at this.

10
00:00:37,074 --> 00:00:38,475
What? What is it?

11
00:00:41,712 --> 00:00:44,481
Oh, it's that case.
The one where the dad was killed...

12
00:00:44,481 --> 00:00:45,949
in front of his daughter
on Christmas night.

13
00:00:45,949 --> 00:00:47,518
He abused his wife and kid...

14
00:00:47,584 --> 00:00:49,887
and ended up stabbing his wife to death
with a soju bottle.

15
00:00:50,154 --> 00:00:51,889
Then seven years later,
right after he was released,

16
00:00:52,756 --> 00:00:53,891
he tried to kill his daughter as well?

17
00:00:54,491 --> 00:00:56,293
That information about the daughter
wasn't released to the press.

18
00:00:56,794 --> 00:01:00,931
She was still a minor at the time,
and possibly...

19
00:01:00,931 --> 00:01:02,332
a witness.

20
00:01:02,966 --> 00:01:05,069
A witness? You mean she saw Kingfisher?

21
00:01:05,702 --> 00:01:09,006
Hey, if she'd seen him, do you think
we'd still be completely in the dark?

22
00:01:11,642 --> 00:01:13,277
Then again, who knows.

23
00:01:13,277 --> 00:01:16,313
Whether she really saw nothing,
or she's just keeping quiet.

24
00:01:17,381 --> 00:01:20,851
The daughter's name was Oh something.
Hang on.

25
00:01:21,685 --> 00:01:23,087
(Incident Report)

26
00:01:32,629 --> 00:01:35,199
Are you crazy? What are you...

27
00:01:36,567 --> 00:01:38,368
I guess you really don't want me to die.

28
00:01:39,503 --> 00:01:43,073
The one and only witness
to Kingfisher's sniping.

29
00:01:44,041 --> 00:01:46,176
The only child I ever showed my face to.

30
00:01:49,146 --> 00:01:50,848
It's been a while, Oh Seung Ah.

31
00:02:06,130 --> 00:02:07,998
Merry Christmas, Yu Bo Na.

32
00:02:08,899 --> 00:02:09,900
Where are the presents?

33
00:02:10,067 --> 00:02:11,902
I'm sure Santa Claus will bring them.

34
00:02:13,237 --> 00:02:15,539
- You think so?
- You never know.

35
00:02:15,539 --> 00:02:17,741
He's known for having a clear sense
of right and wrong.

36
00:02:18,008 --> 00:02:19,510
You've got it wrong too.

37
00:02:19,676 --> 00:02:21,612
You're a terrible boss
for making me work on a day like this.

38
00:02:21,745 --> 00:02:23,514
It's not like you have anything
better to do.

39
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:25,682
Got any friends? A boyfriend? Family?

40
00:02:26,350 --> 00:02:27,818
Just cooped up in a place like this
all by yourself.

41
00:02:28,819 --> 00:02:31,455
But these are all romance comics?

42
00:02:32,489 --> 00:02:33,791
Are you seeing someone lately?

43
00:02:33,791 --> 00:02:35,793
You should head home early.
Your kids are waiting for you.

44
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:38,629
It's not like a few days
will matter for a bastard like him.

45
00:02:38,662 --> 00:02:39,663
That bastard...

46
00:02:40,364 --> 00:02:41,799
could kill someone.

47
00:02:48,472 --> 00:02:50,474
But don't you think he could have changed?

48
00:02:50,941 --> 00:02:52,276
He's still her father.

49
00:02:52,276 --> 00:02:53,444
I know.

50
00:02:53,444 --> 00:02:57,314
To second-guess things
but hold on to hope until the very end.

51
00:02:57,314 --> 00:02:58,816
That's the Yu Bo Na way.

52
00:02:59,583 --> 00:03:01,785
If you want to observe him
for a few more days, go ahead.

53
00:03:01,819 --> 00:03:05,022
Just don't miss your window.

54
00:03:07,424 --> 00:03:10,160
It's cold out, so take a hand warmer.

55
00:03:10,728 --> 00:03:11,729
I'm leaving.

56
00:03:12,963 --> 00:03:14,598
(Crime Scene, Residence At The Time)

57
00:03:16,533 --> 00:03:18,368
(Oh Seung Ah's Daily Route)

58
00:03:24,742 --> 00:03:26,143
(2011 Christmas Flea Market)

59
00:03:39,022 --> 00:03:40,958
I thought that day would be
the last day of my life,

60
00:03:42,192 --> 00:03:43,961
my last Christmas.

61
00:03:44,661 --> 00:03:45,696
That's what I was thinking.

62
00:03:48,232 --> 00:03:50,234
I thought I'd never see this again.

63
00:03:51,869 --> 00:03:53,036
Either I'd die...

64
00:03:54,238 --> 00:03:55,272
or I'd kill.

65
00:03:57,474 --> 00:03:59,743
Right, that must have been why.

66
00:04:01,111 --> 00:04:02,179
Because I could hear your heart.

67
00:04:10,821 --> 00:04:12,623
Do you want a Christmas present?

68
00:04:16,860 --> 00:04:18,062
Then you can't cry.

69
00:04:19,430 --> 00:04:20,764
You have to be good.

70
00:04:22,433 --> 00:04:25,102
I heard that Santa fellow
has a very clear sense of right and wrong.

71
00:04:26,437 --> 00:04:27,738
Who are you?

72
00:04:27,771 --> 00:04:29,039
When you get home,

73
00:04:30,007 --> 00:04:31,542
leave the living room window
open a little.

74
00:04:38,615 --> 00:04:39,616
Let's see each other again.

75
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:46,056
Manager Yu,
what do you think you're doing?

76
00:04:46,056 --> 00:04:48,058
What are you trying to do,
showing your face like that?

77
00:04:56,734 --> 00:04:57,901
Does she think she's Santa?

78
00:04:59,603 --> 00:05:01,739
She doesn't even know what I wished for.

79
00:05:20,257 --> 00:05:22,426
I prayed that I would die sooner.

80
00:05:23,293 --> 00:05:26,797
I begged that if there was a god,
to please let me escape from this hell.

81
00:05:27,631 --> 00:05:28,732
Right at that moment...

82
00:05:38,942 --> 00:05:40,611
...a god really did appear.

83
00:05:54,958 --> 00:05:56,093
The reason I came back.

84
00:05:58,028 --> 00:06:00,664
The reason I do this work.

85
00:06:02,633 --> 00:06:04,401
Hoping that I can save even one person.

86
00:06:06,103 --> 00:06:09,640
Hoping someone will be safe
because of this.

87
00:06:13,143 --> 00:06:14,311
You knew...

88
00:06:16,447 --> 00:06:18,248
You knew everything from the beginning,
so why?

89
00:06:21,185 --> 00:06:22,252
Because I was disappointed.

90
00:06:23,921 --> 00:06:25,322
That girl...

91
00:06:26,857 --> 00:06:27,991
I hoped she'd be like everyone else.

92
00:06:29,126 --> 00:06:32,329
I wanted her to be ordinary and happy,
but she wasn't.

93
00:06:34,598 --> 00:06:36,300
I didn't like the choice you made.

94
00:06:39,403 --> 00:06:40,404
I...

95
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:45,442
I wanted to be like you.

96
00:06:47,311 --> 00:06:49,747
I wanted to stand beside you one day,

97
00:06:51,181 --> 00:06:54,385
and that one dream is why I've worked
myself to death until now.

98
00:06:58,989 --> 00:07:00,090
You shouldn't have.

99
00:07:00,924 --> 00:07:02,393
You should have just gone your own way.

100
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:04,728
Down a safe and bright path.

101
00:07:12,202 --> 00:07:14,304
But you said we'd see each other again.

102
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,041
What?

103
00:07:22,479 --> 00:07:23,547
We'll see each other again.

104
00:07:23,881 --> 00:07:27,484
No, I just meant
that I hoped you'd be safe.

105
00:07:27,484 --> 00:07:30,421
I don't know about that.
Anyway, you have to take responsibility.

106
00:07:31,055 --> 00:07:33,891
Me? You're still just a kid.

107
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:37,361
What's with you?

108
00:07:40,330 --> 00:07:42,232
You were the gift I desperately wanted.

109
00:07:43,934 --> 00:07:45,135
You're my Santa Claus.

110
00:07:46,203 --> 00:07:47,438
The savior of my life.

111
00:07:51,008 --> 00:07:52,142
So take responsibility.

112
00:07:53,210 --> 00:07:55,079
And you're the one who drugged my husband?

113
00:07:56,714 --> 00:07:58,449
It wasn't poison, just a sleeping pill.

114
00:07:59,483 --> 00:08:01,118
Would Kingfisher really be fooled
by something like that?

115
00:08:01,852 --> 00:08:03,620
I knew it was a sleeping pill.

116
00:08:04,688 --> 00:08:06,323
If you knew, why did you bring a gun?

117
00:08:06,356 --> 00:08:07,825
The bullets were real too.

118
00:08:08,459 --> 00:08:09,660
And you were really shooting.

119
00:08:10,294 --> 00:08:13,530
That's because you messed with someone
you shouldn't have.

120
00:08:16,567 --> 00:08:17,568
Darn it.

121
00:08:19,970 --> 00:08:21,238
Such a troublemaker.

122
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:37,688
You've been busy.

123
00:08:40,424 --> 00:08:41,525
So this is when it started?

124
00:08:48,532 --> 00:08:50,467
You didn't like the choice I made either?

125
00:08:51,535 --> 00:08:52,803
About six years ago.

126
00:08:53,270 --> 00:08:55,406
(6 Years Ago)

127
00:08:59,877 --> 00:09:01,879
- I saw you by chance.
- Honey.

128
00:09:02,613 --> 00:09:04,214
I recognized you at a glance.

129
00:09:05,783 --> 00:09:07,618
I haven't forgotten you
for a single day since then.

130
00:09:16,126 --> 00:09:18,395
It felt like my heart
had a hole punched through it.

131
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:21,865
The person who was a god
and a hero to me...

132
00:09:22,533 --> 00:09:25,369
seemed to have become
just an ordinary, weak woman.

133
00:09:26,003 --> 00:09:27,237
You're definitely an anti-fan.

134
00:09:30,507 --> 00:09:31,508
So?

135
00:09:32,810 --> 00:09:34,178
I want to turn you back.

136
00:09:34,211 --> 00:09:36,814
Back into the old Kingfisher.
Back into the person I used to know.

137
00:09:38,849 --> 00:09:41,618
You're a troublemaker, all right.
I thought I told you.

138
00:09:42,019 --> 00:09:44,988
You made your choice,
and I told you I respect it.

139
00:09:45,456 --> 00:09:47,558
Even if I don't like it, it's your life.

140
00:09:48,392 --> 00:09:49,893
I just did my job,

141
00:09:49,927 --> 00:09:53,130
and how you lived your life after that
was your choice to make.

142
00:09:53,130 --> 00:09:54,498
But Kingfisher is...

143
00:09:56,233 --> 00:09:58,168
You seem to be misunderstanding something.

144
00:09:59,236 --> 00:10:00,904
If I'm your savior,

145
00:10:02,005 --> 00:10:04,341
the one who saved Kingfisher
was Kwon Tae Sung.

146
00:10:06,110 --> 00:10:07,144
It was him.

147
00:10:09,747 --> 00:10:10,814
That man...

148
00:10:12,416 --> 00:10:13,884
Did he save your life?

149
00:10:15,285 --> 00:10:16,387
He saved something much bigger.

150
00:10:19,790 --> 00:10:21,191
And I received an even greater gift.

151
00:10:42,946 --> 00:10:44,381
It's Yu Bo Na.

152
00:10:46,350 --> 00:10:47,918
Honey, do you know
where you are right now?

153
00:10:48,719 --> 00:10:49,953
A cafe.

154
00:10:53,157 --> 00:10:56,060
In all my life...
Not even a bar, but a cafe...

155
00:10:56,093 --> 00:10:59,096
They called me to come pick up my husband
because they were closing.

156
00:10:59,997 --> 00:11:01,098
What is going on?

157
00:11:05,569 --> 00:11:07,805
Did I fall asleep? Why? How?

158
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:11,942
But... When did I fall asleep?

159
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:17,681
It's nighttime.

160
00:11:22,186 --> 00:11:23,187
Our date...

161
00:11:24,354 --> 00:11:27,124
Well, our date's over.
What are you going to do about this?

162
00:11:30,761 --> 00:11:32,029
I'm sorry. I...

163
00:11:33,130 --> 00:11:35,566
I'll do all the dishes for one month.
I'm really sorry.

164
00:11:38,335 --> 00:11:39,737
And you think that will be enough?

165
00:11:43,707 --> 00:11:44,708
It won't?

166
00:11:45,209 --> 00:11:47,978
I'll also take Yul
to daycare for one month.

167
00:11:48,746 --> 00:11:49,747
I'm really sorry.

168
00:11:50,581 --> 00:11:52,116
Okay. I'll take your offer.

169
00:11:52,616 --> 00:11:54,385
And for one month,

170
00:11:54,985 --> 00:11:57,521
you'll read one storybook
to Yul every day.

171
00:11:58,355 --> 00:11:59,556
Okay, okay. Deal.

172
00:12:00,090 --> 00:12:01,392
- Okay?
- Okay.

173
00:12:01,392 --> 00:12:03,026
- Deal.
- I'm really sorry.

174
00:12:03,427 --> 00:12:05,129
We wasted all this precious time
because of me.

175
00:12:05,162 --> 00:12:07,431
Really, I'll make it up to you.
I'll make it up to you big time.

176
00:12:11,168 --> 00:12:14,071
What are you going to do?
Honey, I'm so embarrassed. Let's just go.

177
00:12:14,471 --> 00:12:16,607
Se Ah keeps calling. Get up, quickly.

178
00:12:18,776 --> 00:12:20,677
- Are you okay?
- Yes, I'm fine. I'm fine.

179
00:12:20,677 --> 00:12:22,112
- Can you walk?
- Yes.

180
00:12:25,349 --> 00:12:27,751
If that had been real poison,

181
00:12:27,785 --> 00:12:29,653
you would have killed me.

182
00:12:31,388 --> 00:12:32,389
Manager Yu.

183
00:12:33,157 --> 00:12:36,527
If I catch you calling me that at work,

184
00:12:38,162 --> 00:12:39,196
you're dead.

185
00:12:41,899 --> 00:12:43,300
At work.

186
00:12:44,701 --> 00:12:46,870
At work.

187
00:12:49,706 --> 00:12:51,141
So I'll see you at work?

188
00:13:15,466 --> 00:13:20,003
Is your family really worth
risking your life for?

189
00:13:20,003 --> 00:13:21,371
- Two, three.
- Two, three.

190
00:13:23,574 --> 00:13:25,375
Mom, I'm hungry.

191
00:13:25,375 --> 00:13:26,643
Are you hungry, Yul?

192
00:13:26,677 --> 00:13:28,612
It's time to eat, Yul. Right?

193
00:13:28,612 --> 00:13:30,414
Since we're out,
should we eat before going home?

194
00:13:30,414 --> 00:13:32,416
Honey, your mom's radish kimchi
turned out amazing.

195
00:13:32,416 --> 00:13:34,385
I just thought you might be tired.

196
00:13:34,385 --> 00:13:36,220
- You were worried I might be tired?
- Yes.

197
00:13:37,221 --> 00:13:39,289
Honey, look at the flowers.
Aren't they beautiful?

198
00:13:39,289 --> 00:13:41,525
- You're more beautiful. Yes.
- Really?

199
00:13:41,525 --> 00:13:43,594
- Is Mommy prettier than the flowers?
- Yes.

200
00:13:43,594 --> 00:13:44,828
- Really?
- Of course.

201
00:13:46,130 --> 00:13:47,364
Your question was wrong.

202
00:13:49,032 --> 00:13:50,334
It's not about risking my life.

203
00:13:51,235 --> 00:13:53,303
My family is my life.

204
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:05,983
So in the end, she saved someone.

205
00:14:06,483 --> 00:14:08,619
If it weren't for Kingfisher,
that girl would've died.

206
00:14:10,054 --> 00:14:12,289
So the bottom line is...

207
00:14:14,224 --> 00:14:16,326
Man, that's just so awesome.

208
00:14:16,326 --> 00:14:18,629
That's why he has over
a million fans, right?

209
00:14:20,197 --> 00:14:22,299
Hey, get a grip.

210
00:14:22,299 --> 00:14:23,400
Is that how a detective should talk?

211
00:14:25,169 --> 00:14:26,170
I'm sorry.

212
00:14:27,604 --> 00:14:32,209
Look, it's true that all the victims
Kingfisher killed were criminals.

213
00:14:32,209 --> 00:14:34,445
But does that justify murder or not?

214
00:14:35,446 --> 00:14:37,715
- It doesn't.
- The law is a social contract.

215
00:14:38,148 --> 00:14:39,416
By breaking that contract,

216
00:14:39,416 --> 00:14:42,119
does that bastard have the right
to personally judge someone, yes or no?

217
00:14:42,786 --> 00:14:44,021
- No, he doesn't.
- Is it our job as cops...

218
00:14:44,021 --> 00:14:45,522
to catch a bastard like that or not?

219
00:14:46,123 --> 00:14:47,558
- We have to.
- How?

220
00:14:50,928 --> 00:14:51,929
Well?

221
00:14:53,063 --> 00:14:55,199
That's the bottom line. Got it?

222
00:14:58,635 --> 00:15:01,138
Get a grip. Snap out of it.

223
00:15:03,607 --> 00:15:05,008
Hey.

224
00:15:05,008 --> 00:15:06,043
Thank you.

225
00:15:06,944 --> 00:15:08,278
Dig through all the files.

226
00:15:08,278 --> 00:15:09,747
All the way to the last case
from four years ago.

227
00:15:10,214 --> 00:15:13,016
You'll see
a whole other side of Kingfisher.

228
00:15:28,599 --> 00:15:33,203
Hey, hey. Don't go too deep in there.
There are snakes.

229
00:15:33,203 --> 00:15:36,540
You have to dig deep to get anything good.

230
00:15:38,609 --> 00:15:41,412
The really good ones...

231
00:15:41,845 --> 00:15:44,581
always hide from people.

232
00:15:52,823 --> 00:15:55,192
What? What is that?

233
00:15:55,225 --> 00:15:57,194
- Is that a snake?
- Over there, over there...

234
00:15:57,961 --> 00:15:59,096
Oh my.

235
00:15:59,830 --> 00:16:01,698
Call the police. Hurry.

236
00:16:02,566 --> 00:16:04,601
(Not Today)

237
00:16:04,601 --> 00:16:06,336
(Social Affairs Desk)

238
00:16:08,072 --> 00:16:09,540
(I'd report a tip about Kingfisher.
Tomorrow 3 p.m., Lafi Cafe)

239
00:16:11,108 --> 00:16:14,044
Excuse me, did anyone come looking for me
while I was asleep?

240
00:16:14,078 --> 00:16:16,580
You're asking if someone came
while you were sleeping?

241
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:17,748
Yes.

242
00:16:17,748 --> 00:16:20,484
Well, I don't think I saw anyone.

243
00:16:23,153 --> 00:16:24,154
A tip about Kingfisher?

244
00:16:24,822 --> 00:16:28,625
You scared me.
Seriously, stop sneaking up on me.

245
00:16:28,625 --> 00:16:31,695
- If it isn't my old buddy, Kwon Tae Sung.
- Come on.

246
00:16:32,229 --> 00:16:33,931
So you've latched onto
the Kingfisher case after all.

247
00:16:33,931 --> 00:16:34,965
I knew it.

248
00:16:34,998 --> 00:16:37,267
A swallow can't just pass by the mill.

249
00:16:40,304 --> 00:16:42,106
It's a sparrow, not a swallow.

250
00:16:42,706 --> 00:16:44,141
If I got it and thought it was usable,

251
00:16:44,141 --> 00:16:45,642
I was going to pass it on
to the reporter in charge.

252
00:16:46,076 --> 00:16:47,277
What is it?

253
00:16:47,311 --> 00:16:50,848
What is it? Is it big? A scoop?

254
00:16:50,848 --> 00:16:52,483
Did that person really not show up?

255
00:16:54,251 --> 00:16:55,986
Or did they come and I just missed them?

256
00:16:57,554 --> 00:16:58,889
I haven't heard from them since.

257
00:16:59,490 --> 00:17:01,692
Was it just a prank?

258
00:17:01,692 --> 00:17:02,693
What are you mumbling about?

259
00:17:05,362 --> 00:17:08,999
But why is my colleague
from the Economics Department, Ko Ji Su...

260
00:17:10,768 --> 00:17:13,270
always slacking off
instead of doing his job?

261
00:17:16,173 --> 00:17:18,609
He got stood up.
Totally stood up.

262
00:17:19,276 --> 00:17:22,579
Hey, how can this guy talk about
being stood up by a source...

263
00:17:22,579 --> 00:17:24,615
with the straight face of our Director?

264
00:17:26,016 --> 00:17:27,017
Get out of here, you jerk.

265
00:17:28,018 --> 00:17:30,521
Cheer up. You got this.

266
00:17:32,189 --> 00:17:33,323
(Social Affairs Desk)

267
00:17:33,323 --> 00:17:36,193
Hello, good morning.

268
00:17:36,193 --> 00:17:37,795
Hello, good morning.

269
00:17:37,828 --> 00:17:39,129
Look at her.

270
00:17:39,129 --> 00:17:40,297
- Hello.
- Good morning.

271
00:17:40,297 --> 00:17:45,069
She's so cheerful. She has no idea
what her boss is like.

272
00:17:45,102 --> 00:17:46,470
(Not Today: In-Depth News)

273
00:17:48,906 --> 00:17:50,607
- Good morning.
- Hey.

274
00:17:50,607 --> 00:17:51,608
Hello.

275
00:17:53,077 --> 00:17:57,948
Tae Sung, I didn't know what you'd like,
so I got one of everything.

276
00:17:57,948 --> 00:17:58,982
Pick whichever one you want.

277
00:18:00,184 --> 00:18:01,785
I'll take this one. Thanks, Hae Na.

278
00:18:03,721 --> 00:18:05,889
I'm fine. I already have a drink.

279
00:18:09,893 --> 00:18:12,062
That's not good.

280
00:18:12,096 --> 00:18:13,530
Thanks for the drink, Hae Na.

281
00:18:13,564 --> 00:18:15,399
Tae Sung is so lucky.

282
00:18:15,866 --> 00:18:17,034
Thanks, Hae Na.

283
00:18:17,034 --> 00:18:19,503
- Thanks, Hae Na.
- You're the best, Hae Na.

284
00:18:32,716 --> 00:18:33,717
Reporter Koo Hae Na.

285
00:18:35,619 --> 00:18:36,620
Yes.

286
00:18:36,653 --> 00:18:40,090
This is a list of potential stories
I've put together for us to cover.

287
00:18:40,090 --> 00:18:41,892
Take a look and let me know
if any of them interest you.

288
00:18:43,026 --> 00:18:44,027
What?

289
00:18:44,061 --> 00:18:46,797
We focus on in-depth reporting
rather than straight news,

290
00:18:46,797 --> 00:18:47,965
so our investigations
take a little longer.

291
00:18:47,998 --> 00:18:50,267
We'll do the reporting together
and split writing the articles.

292
00:18:52,035 --> 00:18:53,036
Okay.

293
00:18:55,372 --> 00:18:57,975
For a reporter,
your research and your articles...

294
00:18:57,975 --> 00:18:59,376
are how you prove yourself.

295
00:19:00,577 --> 00:19:01,578
You know that, right?

296
00:19:10,421 --> 00:19:11,422
What was that about?

297
00:19:11,422 --> 00:19:15,359
What a mysterious guy,
running so hot and cold.

298
00:19:17,995 --> 00:19:19,496
(Accidents Act, Site Checks,
Released Child Offenders)

299
00:19:19,963 --> 00:19:20,964
(Prison Overcrowding And Parole)

300
00:19:23,467 --> 00:19:26,670
When a reporter is digging deep
into a case or a person...

301
00:19:26,670 --> 00:19:28,539
and then suddenly drops it all,

302
00:19:29,373 --> 00:19:30,507
it's one of two things.

303
00:19:31,308 --> 00:19:33,477
Either they were paid off,
or they were threatened.

304
00:19:36,046 --> 00:19:38,415
Who was paid off or threatened?

305
00:19:39,483 --> 00:19:41,518
If it were me, I'd take the money.

306
00:19:42,119 --> 00:19:44,955
But he doesn't seem like the type
to be swayed by either.

307
00:19:47,991 --> 00:19:51,161
(Not Today: In-Depth News)

308
00:19:52,730 --> 00:19:55,833
But it looks like
the spark isn't dead yet.

309
00:19:57,201 --> 00:19:58,669
(Durumi Electronics)

310
00:19:58,702 --> 00:19:59,903
(Sales Team 3)

311
00:20:03,507 --> 00:20:04,675
Good morning.

312
00:20:05,509 --> 00:20:06,844
(Sales Team 3)

313
00:20:09,213 --> 00:20:10,214
(Team Leader Kim Bong Pal)

314
00:20:11,181 --> 00:20:13,350
- Good morning.
- Thank you, morning candy.

315
00:20:13,350 --> 00:20:16,820
- Thank you. Good morning.
- Thank you.

316
00:20:16,820 --> 00:20:18,322
- Good morning.
- Hello.

317
00:20:31,735 --> 00:20:32,803
(Client List)

318
00:20:39,243 --> 00:20:40,677
(Client Report)

319
00:20:40,711 --> 00:20:41,712
Gold.

320
00:20:41,712 --> 00:20:43,580
(Gold: Used money and power
to evade the law)

321
00:20:43,614 --> 00:20:44,782
White.

322
00:20:44,782 --> 00:20:46,216
(White: Targeted children and adolescents)

323
00:20:46,216 --> 00:20:47,217
Black.

324
00:20:47,818 --> 00:20:48,819
Gray.

325
00:20:50,454 --> 00:20:51,488
Finish.

326
00:21:02,266 --> 00:21:03,300
Of course, Detective Lee is here.

327
00:21:03,867 --> 00:21:04,868
Yes.

328
00:21:05,402 --> 00:21:06,804
You got pulled in
because of your record, right?

329
00:21:08,605 --> 00:21:10,808
Thanks for your work on this.

330
00:21:10,808 --> 00:21:13,310
- Record? What record?
- You didn't know?

331
00:21:14,111 --> 00:21:17,314
Five years ago, he took down
the Oh Seon Il organ trafficking ring.

332
00:21:17,314 --> 00:21:18,315
That was all Detective Lee.

333
00:21:18,882 --> 00:21:21,151
That case was huge back then. Incredible.

334
00:21:21,785 --> 00:21:24,254
So that's why the chief...

335
00:21:24,254 --> 00:21:26,557
Are they missing this time too?

336
00:21:26,557 --> 00:21:27,725
Yes, they are gone.

337
00:21:28,992 --> 00:21:31,662
Lungs, heart, liver, kidneys,
and pancreas.

338
00:21:32,196 --> 00:21:33,230
They took them all.

339
00:21:34,098 --> 00:21:37,501
Judging by the rate of decomposition,
it's been about 3 or 4 weeks.

340
00:21:38,402 --> 00:21:41,004
Well, they could have buried him
in the winter,

341
00:21:41,004 --> 00:21:42,806
and it could have been uncovered
when the weather got warmer.

342
00:21:45,142 --> 00:21:46,777
I thought things had quieted down.

343
00:21:47,411 --> 00:21:49,780
Still,

344
00:21:50,347 --> 00:21:52,216
to think they roughly stitched him up
before dumping him...

345
00:21:53,016 --> 00:21:54,918
This isn't a game.

346
00:21:55,953 --> 00:21:58,622
These guys seem even more vicious
than the last ones.

347
00:21:59,356 --> 00:22:02,192
Detective Lee,
you've got your work cut out for you.

348
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:04,161
Yes.

349
00:22:08,399 --> 00:22:10,401
Beom, what's our first step?

350
00:22:10,901 --> 00:22:14,405
The victim was hiking Mount Taegong
when he was reported missing.

351
00:22:14,405 --> 00:22:16,573
So I'll check with the precinct in charge
about the original investigation.

352
00:22:16,573 --> 00:22:19,943
Do that. And secure the CCTV footage
from the hiking trail at the time.

353
00:22:19,943 --> 00:22:22,279
Yes. And as for Mount Cheongri
where the body was found,

354
00:22:22,279 --> 00:22:24,148
I'll request their assistance
with the canvass.

355
00:22:24,148 --> 00:22:25,149
Hey, Beom.

356
00:22:26,016 --> 00:22:27,084
You seem excited.

357
00:22:27,084 --> 00:22:28,685
(Forensic Imaging Lab)

358
00:22:28,685 --> 00:22:30,354
Well, there's a lot to dig into
with this one.

359
00:22:30,387 --> 00:22:32,356
And these guys are bastards,
so it'll be satisfying to catch them.

360
00:22:34,158 --> 00:22:36,293
Check if there are any other
missing persons cases...

361
00:22:36,293 --> 00:22:37,828
reported around Mount Taegong.

362
00:22:37,828 --> 00:22:39,763
And search the database...

363
00:22:39,763 --> 00:22:42,132
to see if there have been
any similar bodies found recently.

364
00:22:42,599 --> 00:22:44,201
What? Why is that?

365
00:22:44,768 --> 00:22:46,804
Someone who went missing
in Gangwon Province...

366
00:22:46,804 --> 00:22:48,839
was found secretly buried in Seoul.

367
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:53,043
They wouldn't go to all that trouble
to get rid of just one person.

368
00:22:53,510 --> 00:22:54,578
Oh.

369
00:22:57,281 --> 00:22:59,183
Hey, Beom, go wait in the car.

370
00:22:59,216 --> 00:23:00,417
I have to stop by somewhere first.

371
00:23:00,951 --> 00:23:02,319
Okay.

372
00:23:02,319 --> 00:23:05,122
(Clinical Laboratory, Histopathology Lab)

373
00:23:05,122 --> 00:23:06,123
Let's do this!

374
00:23:09,393 --> 00:23:10,928
- You're here?
- Of course.

375
00:23:24,441 --> 00:23:26,176
Oh, my. Hey.

376
00:23:28,045 --> 00:23:30,581
Manager Yu, good morning.

377
00:23:30,614 --> 00:23:32,049
Yes, Ms. Oh Hyun Nam.

378
00:23:33,016 --> 00:23:34,218
- You're here?
- Yes.

379
00:23:36,420 --> 00:23:37,821
Let's see here.

380
00:23:38,322 --> 00:23:40,624
My, my, we have four submissions today?

381
00:23:41,825 --> 00:23:44,695
Black, Gray, and Gold.

382
00:23:47,831 --> 00:23:48,866
It's been a while,

383
00:23:50,467 --> 00:23:51,602
but White is here too.

384
00:23:59,243 --> 00:24:02,546
All right, all right.
The new Client List is in,

385
00:24:02,546 --> 00:24:04,581
so let's have a productive meeting.

386
00:24:05,182 --> 00:24:06,417
- Yes, sir.
- Okay.

387
00:24:06,417 --> 00:24:07,584
My goodness.

388
00:24:08,285 --> 00:24:10,354
Someone go get Bong Tae Min.

389
00:24:11,388 --> 00:24:14,925
Wow, this Client is a bit much, right?

390
00:24:14,925 --> 00:24:18,962
- The next ones aren't any easier.
- This month is going to be so tough.

391
00:24:19,563 --> 00:24:20,931
I'll go get him.

392
00:24:20,964 --> 00:24:21,965
I will.

393
00:24:22,833 --> 00:24:24,034
I'll be right back.

394
00:24:26,637 --> 00:24:28,539
That room is basically
a chemical hazard zone.

395
00:24:28,939 --> 00:24:29,940
Will she be okay?

396
00:24:30,507 --> 00:24:32,076
We should have given her a mask.

397
00:24:32,109 --> 00:24:35,279
She's been trained with all sorts
of chemicals, so if anything...

398
00:24:36,213 --> 00:24:37,381
She might enjoy it.

399
00:24:39,516 --> 00:24:40,584
Three.

400
00:24:40,617 --> 00:24:41,819
Two.

401
00:24:45,322 --> 00:24:46,323
Darn it.

402
00:24:48,692 --> 00:24:49,760
Darn.

403
00:25:01,839 --> 00:25:03,741
This is the work of a top-class expert.

404
00:25:04,208 --> 00:25:06,276
You could even call it genius.

405
00:25:07,678 --> 00:25:08,912
I did some digging,

406
00:25:08,912 --> 00:25:11,115
and as expected,
there are no guns in the country...

407
00:25:11,115 --> 00:25:12,116
that use this kind of bullet.

408
00:25:12,116 --> 00:25:13,984
I can't even find any abroad.

409
00:25:14,685 --> 00:25:18,555
That means someone
must have custom-made it.

410
00:25:19,390 --> 00:25:20,824
It's been that way since the first case.

411
00:25:21,458 --> 00:25:22,926
It looked like the bullet was
different this time,

412
00:25:22,926 --> 00:25:24,395
so I asked just in case.

413
00:25:24,395 --> 00:25:27,097
It means they upgrade their equipment
every few years.

414
00:25:27,765 --> 00:25:30,000
But for a technician
of that Special S-Class caliber...

415
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:31,368
there's no way I wouldn't know about them.

416
00:25:31,902 --> 00:25:34,805
Could Kingfisher be making
the guns himself?

417
00:25:34,805 --> 00:25:36,306
No, I don't think
he's making them himself.

418
00:25:36,740 --> 00:25:38,942
True, considering the times we live in.

419
00:25:38,942 --> 00:25:41,979
He must have a smart helper or two.

420
00:25:42,379 --> 00:25:45,416
It could be 1 or 2,
or it could be a whole team.

421
00:25:46,183 --> 00:25:49,820
And just like you said, sir,
they could all be Special S-Class experts.

422
00:25:57,127 --> 00:25:58,495
She'll be right back out.

423
00:26:03,534 --> 00:26:04,835
Don't get on.

424
00:26:05,302 --> 00:26:07,571
- Don't get on.
- Don't get on.

425
00:26:07,571 --> 00:26:09,440
- Don't get on.
- Let's not get on.

426
00:26:09,973 --> 00:26:12,776
- Gosh, what a weasel.
- It's not crowded. Let's get on.

427
00:26:15,879 --> 00:26:17,381
- Excuse me.
- Coming through.

428
00:26:17,381 --> 00:26:19,550
- We're getting on.
- Excuse me. Excuse me.

429
00:26:28,425 --> 00:26:29,827
I see a new face.

430
00:26:29,827 --> 00:26:31,061
Well, she is...

431
00:26:31,695 --> 00:26:33,597
the rookie who joined my team.

432
00:26:34,264 --> 00:26:36,066
I see. The one who just joined?

433
00:26:37,201 --> 00:26:39,603
Wow, what bad luck.

434
00:26:39,603 --> 00:26:42,339
For a salesperson, it's important
to get off on the right foot.

435
00:26:42,372 --> 00:26:43,874
Well, the timing is good, at least.

436
00:26:44,308 --> 00:26:46,410
You know we've set a date for
the entire Sales Team workshop, right?

437
00:26:47,044 --> 00:26:48,245
Team Leader Bong, I'm counting on you.

438
00:26:50,314 --> 00:26:51,315
Of course.

439
00:26:51,915 --> 00:26:54,551
Does just adding more people
improve our sales numbers?

440
00:26:55,052 --> 00:26:57,755
Even with a small, elite team...
It's about skills.

441
00:26:58,322 --> 00:27:01,358
The 1-shot, 1-kill sales technique
of silently closing in,

442
00:27:01,358 --> 00:27:03,394
striking, and getting out.

443
00:27:07,231 --> 00:27:09,233
Should I set a date and give
a special lecture or something?

444
00:27:09,767 --> 00:27:11,535
- I know, right?
- Enjoy your lunch.

445
00:27:16,907 --> 00:27:18,242
That jerk. My goodness.

446
00:27:21,211 --> 00:27:23,480
Hey, hey. Let's go get some food.

447
00:27:25,582 --> 00:27:26,583
Here.

448
00:27:29,339 --> 00:27:32,710
This is great. Hey, get a three-tier cake.

449
00:27:32,710 --> 00:27:35,779
- I'll take care of that.
- As expected.

450
00:27:35,779 --> 00:27:37,414
Yes, I'll prepare a three-tier cake.

451
00:27:37,414 --> 00:27:38,849
You need to understand, Hyun Nam.

452
00:27:40,150 --> 00:27:41,552
In sales,

453
00:27:42,419 --> 00:27:44,822
your performance is your rank and status.

454
00:27:44,822 --> 00:27:47,591
It must be hard working here, right?

455
00:27:47,624 --> 00:27:48,726
Right?

456
00:27:49,593 --> 00:27:51,295
Speaking of which, Team Leader.

457
00:27:51,328 --> 00:27:52,963
Since our sales numbers are fake anyway,

458
00:27:52,963 --> 00:27:55,632
- do we have to be last place every time?
- What...

459
00:27:55,666 --> 00:27:57,368
I mean, we don't have to be number one,

460
00:27:57,368 --> 00:27:59,903
- but maybe third place sometimes...
- Hey.

461
00:28:01,171 --> 00:28:04,875
So many people are working their tails off
just to sell one more fan.

462
00:28:04,875 --> 00:28:06,343
It's right for us to be at the bottom.

463
00:28:07,711 --> 00:28:11,181
We can't disrespect the people
who work so hard every day.

464
00:28:13,250 --> 00:28:14,318
Right.

465
00:28:14,318 --> 00:28:16,587
Then for next month,
I'll post a negative value...

466
00:28:16,587 --> 00:28:18,055
based on the lowest numbers
from each team.

467
00:28:22,559 --> 00:28:25,562
But do we really have to
go to the workshop?

468
00:28:25,562 --> 00:28:26,930
Isn't that a bit much?

469
00:28:27,531 --> 00:28:28,532
Normally, we wouldn't go.

470
00:28:28,565 --> 00:28:32,770
We don't go, but this time,
since Hyun Nam just joined...

471
00:28:32,803 --> 00:28:34,204
It's just the way it is, you know?

472
00:28:35,139 --> 00:28:37,608
It's a team-building event, and we can all
get some fresh air for a change.

473
00:28:37,608 --> 00:28:39,043
I think it's a good opportunity.

474
00:28:39,043 --> 00:28:40,878
Don't you know a workshop is
an extension of work?

475
00:28:44,982 --> 00:28:47,351
Like we have anything to talk about
with fan salespeople.

476
00:28:49,353 --> 00:28:50,621
That sounds fun.

477
00:28:50,654 --> 00:28:51,922
I've never been to one.

478
00:28:52,856 --> 00:28:54,224
I'm really looking forward to it.

479
00:28:54,958 --> 00:28:56,026
I can't wait to go.

480
00:29:02,433 --> 00:29:05,502
But are you okay with that, Manager Yu?
It's an overnight trip.

481
00:29:05,502 --> 00:29:06,503
That's true.

482
00:29:08,405 --> 00:29:10,140
Let's go.

483
00:29:10,140 --> 00:29:11,175
(Durumi Electronics)

484
00:29:11,208 --> 00:29:13,243
Wow, Team Leader Kim,
that actually looks good on you.

485
00:29:13,243 --> 00:29:15,245
Really? I'll give it to you
after the workshop.

486
00:29:15,279 --> 00:29:16,947
Still, wearing matching outfits
makes it feel...

487
00:29:16,947 --> 00:29:18,449
like we're really going on a trip, right?

488
00:29:20,718 --> 00:29:21,719
Mom.

489
00:29:22,453 --> 00:29:25,823
Yul. Are you off to daycare now?

490
00:29:25,823 --> 00:29:29,359
- Yes.
- Yul and I just finished getting ready.

491
00:29:29,393 --> 00:29:32,162
We're heading out. Let's go.

492
00:29:33,263 --> 00:29:35,299
Oh, but honey,
are you sure you'll be okay on your own?

493
00:29:35,833 --> 00:29:39,203
Maybe I should call Se Ah
and ask her to help out tonight?

494
00:29:39,236 --> 00:29:42,606
It's fine. I can handle it on my own.

495
00:29:42,606 --> 00:29:45,876
Don't worry about us
and just go have a great time.

496
00:29:45,909 --> 00:29:48,946
Okay, thank you. I will.

497
00:29:49,780 --> 00:29:52,816
Sweetheart, why don't you say
"have a good trip" to Mom?

498
00:29:54,551 --> 00:29:55,552
Mom, when are you coming back?

499
00:29:56,186 --> 00:29:57,654
Yul, that's not what we talked about.

500
00:29:57,654 --> 00:30:00,023
Sweetie, I'm only staying for one night.

501
00:30:00,023 --> 00:30:01,759
Just one night.
I told you, remember? Right?

502
00:30:02,159 --> 00:30:03,394
Yes? Yul?

503
00:30:03,394 --> 00:30:05,596
You'll be a good girl for Dad
while I'm away, right?

504
00:30:05,629 --> 00:30:07,264
Mom, where are you going?

505
00:30:08,265 --> 00:30:09,400
Well...

506
00:30:10,034 --> 00:30:11,035
Honey, just a second.

507
00:30:11,668 --> 00:30:15,939
Yul, you have to do what we practiced.
Sweetheart, say goodbye to your mom.

508
00:30:17,541 --> 00:30:19,910
Mom, have a safe trip.

509
00:30:19,943 --> 00:30:22,112
A big salute.

510
00:30:22,513 --> 00:30:23,547
Salute.

511
00:30:24,982 --> 00:30:27,518
Salute. I'm heading out.

512
