- Let's start getting ready.

760
00:44:56,679 --> 00:44:57,680
Okay.

761
00:44:58,281 --> 00:45:00,550
- Hey, get your tools, okay?
- Yes, sir.

762
00:45:02,719 --> 00:45:03,820
Get ready.

763
00:45:07,557 --> 00:45:09,092
Time to go hunting.

764
00:45:17,066 --> 00:45:18,368
Put them over here.

765
00:45:19,002 --> 00:45:23,706
Oh my, a lot of you
are already passed out.

766
00:45:24,941 --> 00:45:27,110
- Here, have some of this.
- Oh, you're here.

767
00:45:27,110 --> 00:45:28,811
When you have an upset stomach
from drinking,

768
00:45:28,811 --> 00:45:30,680
this honey water is the best thing for it.

769
00:45:30,680 --> 00:45:32,415
- Yes, thank you.
- Thank you.

770
00:45:32,415 --> 00:45:33,650
- Thank you.
- Everyone, have a glass.

771
00:45:33,650 --> 00:45:35,118
- Drink it all down.
- Have some.

772
00:45:35,118 --> 00:45:36,553
Excuse me. Wait, just a second.

773
00:45:37,186 --> 00:45:41,024
I wonder which one of these
has the most honey in it?

774
00:45:41,724 --> 00:45:42,725
Could it be this one?

775
00:45:42,725 --> 00:45:46,029
I'll take this one.

776
00:45:46,062 --> 00:45:47,630
Then I'll...

777
00:45:48,831 --> 00:45:51,000
- I wonder if this one has more?
- Yes, go ahead.

778
00:45:51,801 --> 00:45:53,536
I'll drink this one.

779
00:45:53,603 --> 00:45:56,239
- Okay.
- Yes, thank you.

780
00:45:56,239 --> 00:45:57,607
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

781
00:45:57,607 --> 00:46:00,910
- Thank you.
- Here, have some of this.

782
00:46:00,910 --> 00:46:03,179
This is all-natural honey.

783
00:46:03,179 --> 00:46:06,049
Yes, thank you so much
for the honey water.

784
00:46:06,082 --> 00:46:08,151
- Yes.
- All right, bottoms up.

785
00:46:08,151 --> 00:46:10,286
- Bottoms up. Bottoms up.
- Bottoms up. Bottoms up.

786
00:46:10,286 --> 00:46:12,255
- Bottoms up. Bottoms up.
- Bottoms up. Bottoms up.

787
00:46:16,626 --> 00:46:17,694
Thank you.

788
00:46:19,195 --> 00:46:22,899
- It's the real deal.
- Well then, you all relax and have fun.

789
00:46:22,899 --> 00:46:24,767
- Okay.
- All right.

790
00:46:25,301 --> 00:46:26,302
Go on.

791
00:46:44,687 --> 00:46:46,256
These bastards are crossing the line.

792
00:46:47,223 --> 00:46:49,959
(Durumi Electronics Sales Team Workshop)

793
00:46:49,993 --> 00:46:53,062
The bastards' hideout is on
the east side of Mount Taegong.

794
00:46:53,530 --> 00:46:55,732
It's presumed to be
the Mount Taegong Old Man Pension.

795
00:47:02,372 --> 00:47:05,542
But as of now,

796
00:47:05,542 --> 00:47:08,111
we don't have any concrete evidence.

797
00:47:09,012 --> 00:47:11,214
You know we've set a date
for the entire Sales Team workshop, right?

798
00:47:12,181 --> 00:47:13,383
Team Leader Bong, I'm counting on you.

799
00:47:15,251 --> 00:47:16,319
Of course.

800
00:47:20,189 --> 00:47:22,392
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

801
00:47:24,627 --> 00:47:25,895
Remember.

802
00:47:25,895 --> 00:47:28,898
Our objective is to gather intel,
not to have a Meeting.

803
00:47:29,832 --> 00:47:32,669
And remember that their safety
is our top priority.

804
00:47:33,236 --> 00:47:35,205
Right.

805
00:47:52,255 --> 00:47:54,757
The building's entire exterior
is fitted with EMP shielding.

806
00:47:55,625 --> 00:47:57,760
It must be to cut off
all outside communication in an emergency.

807
00:48:47,610 --> 00:48:48,678
Bingo.

808
00:48:48,678 --> 00:48:50,046
Excuse me. Wait, just a second.

809
00:48:50,046 --> 00:48:54,250
I wonder which one of these
has the most honey in it?

810
00:48:54,884 --> 00:48:57,287
It's not dangerous. Just a sleeping pill.

811
00:48:57,287 --> 00:48:58,888
I'll drink this one.

812
00:49:00,957 --> 00:49:02,158
It's a neutralizing agent for the drug.

813
00:49:05,862 --> 00:49:08,631
They've never messed with
the guests before.

814
00:49:09,232 --> 00:49:10,700
I guess they've lost their minds.

815
00:49:10,733 --> 00:49:12,769
The police are onto them,
so they're getting desperate.

816
00:49:12,769 --> 00:49:15,004
They're trying to pull
one last big job and skip town.

817
00:49:15,038 --> 00:49:16,573
We'll keep an eye on
the situation for now.

818
00:49:17,173 --> 00:49:19,008
By the way,
I haven't seen Tae Min in a while.

819
00:49:19,008 --> 00:49:21,211
Assistant Manager Ki said
the signal was bad and went outside.

820
00:49:21,211 --> 00:49:22,912
My cell phone's not working either.

821
00:49:22,912 --> 00:49:24,581
I think they turned on that device.

822
00:49:24,581 --> 00:49:25,582
Darn.

823
00:49:26,716 --> 00:49:27,717
I'll go out and look for them.

824
00:49:32,322 --> 00:49:34,424
Please take good care of
Manager Yu for me.

825
00:49:34,457 --> 00:49:35,592
I got it. Just hurry back.

826
00:49:44,567 --> 00:49:45,802
Assistant Manager Ki.

827
00:49:46,803 --> 00:49:48,037
Manager Tae Min.

828
00:49:49,439 --> 00:49:51,040
Where are they?

829
00:49:53,176 --> 00:49:54,310
Assistant Manager Ki.

830
00:49:55,245 --> 00:49:56,646
Manager Tae Min.

831
00:49:57,480 --> 00:49:58,648
Seriously.

832
00:49:59,382 --> 00:50:01,150
Unbelievable...

833
00:50:24,707 --> 00:50:26,175
What are they holding?

834
00:50:31,915 --> 00:50:35,652
Wow, look how much this is all worth.
We hit the jackpot today.

835
00:50:37,153 --> 00:50:38,421
Tie them all up!

836
00:50:38,922 --> 00:50:39,923
- Okay.
- Yes, sir!

837
00:50:41,858 --> 00:50:44,527
It's a good thing
they're out from the sleeping pills.

838
00:50:45,628 --> 00:50:46,996
Those psychos.

839
00:50:47,564 --> 00:50:50,099
Let's leave the psychos for now
and find Assistant Manager Ki.

840
00:50:51,034 --> 00:50:53,269
I haven't been able to reach him.
He must've gotten caught.

841
00:50:55,471 --> 00:50:56,573
I wonder if he's already dead.

842
00:50:57,507 --> 00:50:58,508
Hey.

843
00:51:00,476 --> 00:51:02,145
If he's alive,
he must be somewhere around here.

844
00:51:02,845 --> 00:51:04,380
Because no cars have left.

845
00:51:13,223 --> 00:51:15,291
Tie them up tight.

846
00:51:15,291 --> 00:51:18,328
Hey, hey, move Ko Yeong Gap
out of the way.

847
00:51:24,000 --> 00:51:25,068
Who are these two?

848
00:51:25,635 --> 00:51:26,836
Why are they okay?

849
00:51:26,836 --> 00:51:27,837
Hey, fellas.

850
00:51:28,671 --> 00:51:31,808
If you keep this up,
you're going to have a problem.

851
00:51:32,775 --> 00:51:34,777
A problem?

852
00:51:34,777 --> 00:51:36,713
You've got to be kidding me.

853
00:51:38,348 --> 00:51:40,917
Old Man, these guys are still awake.
What do we do?

854
00:51:41,751 --> 00:51:43,453
- Kill them?
- Are you nuts? Goodness.

855
00:51:47,523 --> 00:51:49,325
They're worth 300 million a head.

856
00:51:49,359 --> 00:51:50,360
Three million a head?

857
00:51:53,696 --> 00:51:56,699
The old lady must've
dropped the ball again.

858
00:51:58,101 --> 00:51:59,102
Tie them up for now.

859
00:51:59,536 --> 00:52:00,637
Or knock them out.

860
00:52:01,471 --> 00:52:04,007
How do you knock someone out?

861
00:52:04,007 --> 00:52:05,608
I don't want to get hurt.

862
00:52:06,309 --> 00:52:10,413
Great, my phone's dead again.
This is a problem, isn't it?

863
00:52:10,413 --> 00:52:13,716
Why? Are you going to
call the cops or something?

864
00:52:13,716 --> 00:52:15,084
What a pathetic joke.

865
00:52:15,084 --> 00:52:18,521
Hey, man, come on. Let's talk this out...

866
00:52:20,089 --> 00:52:21,424
- My goodness.
- Mr. Kim.

867
00:52:21,424 --> 00:52:22,692
You want to talk with your fists?

868
00:52:22,725 --> 00:52:25,428
- This son of a gun...
- I was itching for a fight anyway.

869
00:52:25,995 --> 00:52:27,363
Don't push your luck.

870
00:52:27,764 --> 00:52:30,033
- Let's just shut up.
- Hey. Careful with your knife.

871
00:52:30,033 --> 00:52:31,434
Please help me.

872
00:52:32,535 --> 00:52:34,003
Please help me.

873
00:52:34,003 --> 00:52:36,206
- Mr. Kim.
- Mr. Kim.

874
00:52:36,206 --> 00:52:37,307
There's a girl over there.

875
00:52:37,907 --> 00:52:39,842
- Go tie her up.
- Tie them all up over here.

876
00:52:43,413 --> 00:52:44,914
You'll regret this.

877
00:52:44,948 --> 00:52:46,082
I'll regret this?

878
00:52:46,149 --> 00:52:48,284
- Mr. Kim.
- Put the knife down.

879
00:52:50,853 --> 00:52:52,322
(Durumi Electronics)

880
00:52:54,624 --> 00:52:55,792
The person
you are trying to reach is unavailable.

881
00:52:55,792 --> 00:52:58,561
You will be connected to their voicemail,
after the beep...

882
00:52:58,595 --> 00:53:00,663
(Red Hat)

883
00:53:00,663 --> 00:53:03,600
What should we do?
Your mom isn't picking up.

884
00:53:03,600 --> 00:53:06,302
I miss Mommy...

885
00:53:07,003 --> 00:53:11,808
Yul, do you miss Mommy?
Daddy misses Mommy a lot too.

886
00:53:11,841 --> 00:53:14,110
Why isn't Mommy answering?

887
00:53:14,143 --> 00:53:17,747
Mommy's in a deep, dark forest right now.

888
00:53:17,747 --> 00:53:19,549
The phones don't work very well there.

889
00:53:19,549 --> 00:53:20,817
A forest?

890
00:53:20,817 --> 00:53:23,052
Then what if Mommy is like
Little Red Riding Hood

891
00:53:23,052 --> 00:53:25,655
and meets a wolf in the forest?

892
00:53:26,222 --> 00:53:27,223
What?

893
00:53:29,492 --> 00:53:30,493
Is it here?

894
00:53:31,327 --> 00:53:32,762
It's padlocked. What should we do?

895
00:54:04,394 --> 00:54:06,162
Assistant Manager Ki, are you in there?

896
00:54:08,498 --> 00:54:09,766
Hey.

897
00:54:25,648 --> 00:54:26,649
What happened?

898
00:54:26,683 --> 00:54:28,518
Did our Assistant Manager Ki
screw up again?

899
00:54:32,722 --> 00:54:34,190
You're always something else.

900
00:54:34,857 --> 00:54:37,627
Shouldn't you at least pretend
to be surprised and worried?

901
00:54:38,561 --> 00:54:40,463
Oh my gosh, what happened? Are you okay?

902
00:54:41,965 --> 00:54:43,266
You two don't get along?

903
00:54:45,034 --> 00:54:47,203
How awful.

904
00:54:47,871 --> 00:54:49,005
How is it inside?

905
00:54:49,005 --> 00:54:50,139
They've already run into each other.

906
00:54:50,940 --> 00:54:52,175
They have got some numbers too.

907
00:54:52,208 --> 00:54:54,811
- Looks like today's the day.
- Shouldn't we hurry in?

908
00:54:54,811 --> 00:54:55,945
They've probably already started fighting.

909
00:54:56,412 --> 00:54:57,413
Mm-hmm.

910
00:55:02,852 --> 00:55:04,554
Mr. Kim.

911
00:55:06,055 --> 00:55:08,091
- I won't let you get away with this.
- Gosh.

912
00:55:11,294 --> 00:55:12,562
Why can't we touch them?

913
00:55:13,396 --> 00:55:14,397
They're Gray.

914
00:55:14,931 --> 00:55:17,467
- What?
- They're not targets for a Meeting yet.

915
00:55:18,701 --> 00:55:20,637
Don't you know that Gray are targets
under investigation...

916
00:55:20,637 --> 00:55:21,838
before they're confirmed as a Client?

917
00:55:22,372 --> 00:55:24,107
I know that much.

918
00:55:24,607 --> 00:55:26,876
But they're the ones
who attacked us first.

919
00:55:26,876 --> 00:55:28,177
Under no circumstances...

920
00:55:28,778 --> 00:55:31,080
can we conduct a Meeting on anyone
who isn't a Client.

921
00:55:32,248 --> 00:55:36,286
We verify and analyze the information
multiple times through the system,

922
00:55:36,920 --> 00:55:39,589
and only then do we handle
the finally approved target.

923
00:55:40,757 --> 00:55:41,824
Those are our rules.

924
00:55:44,227 --> 00:55:46,930
So we just sit here and take this?
There are other people in there too.

925
00:55:47,497 --> 00:55:49,832
Don't you worry. I did say "not yet."

926
00:55:51,868 --> 00:55:53,703
Tie them tightly.

927
00:55:53,703 --> 00:55:54,971
Take them now.

928
00:55:55,972 --> 00:55:57,240
Get rid of this.

929
00:56:01,678 --> 00:56:03,846
Are you okay, Mr. Kim?

930
00:56:06,049 --> 00:56:07,317
I'm fine.

931
00:56:08,218 --> 00:56:11,487
They're not actually going to
kill us, right?

932
00:56:11,988 --> 00:56:16,326
- Yes, we are.
- Really? How are you going to kill us?

933
00:56:16,359 --> 00:56:17,493
How should I kill you?

934
00:56:18,561 --> 00:56:21,631
- For you, I'll do something special.
- Come on.

935
00:56:21,631 --> 00:56:22,899
No, wait.

936
00:56:23,366 --> 00:56:25,034
Seeing those bright, shiny eyes,

937
00:56:25,068 --> 00:56:26,236
I think I'll start by gouging them out.

938
00:56:26,736 --> 00:56:27,804
They still look in good shape.

939
00:56:28,171 --> 00:56:31,341
That's right. My eyes are my best feature.

940
00:56:31,941 --> 00:56:34,611
I eat a lot of lettuce. Beta-carotene.

941
00:56:36,446 --> 00:56:38,147
Beta-what?

942
00:56:38,181 --> 00:56:40,183
Beta-carotene, you idiot.

943
00:56:40,183 --> 00:56:41,317
You little...

944
00:56:41,885 --> 00:56:43,720
Why are you even playing along with him?

945
00:56:43,753 --> 00:56:46,289
Enough of this nonsense.
Move them to the warehouse, now.

946
00:56:46,322 --> 00:56:47,690
And call Dr. Jo.

947
00:56:48,358 --> 00:56:50,126
Tell him to come in
first thing in the morning.

948
00:56:50,159 --> 00:56:51,761
Contact our Clients.

949
00:56:54,531 --> 00:56:55,865
They're going to love this.

950
00:56:56,833 --> 00:56:59,135
They're all so young and fresh.

951
00:57:01,337 --> 00:57:03,339
I think we're really going to die.
What do we do?

952
00:57:03,373 --> 00:57:05,008
Don't worry.

953
00:57:05,041 --> 00:57:07,577
My fortune says I'll live to be 150.

954
00:57:09,812 --> 00:57:11,180
Bullshit.

955
00:57:11,214 --> 00:57:14,450
But what the hell has that bastard
been staring at this whole time?

956
00:57:14,450 --> 00:57:16,686
The phone, you idiot. That phone.

957
00:57:16,719 --> 00:57:18,688
But there's no signal on the phone.

958
00:57:19,689 --> 00:57:20,857
(Danger Authorized Personnel Only)

959
00:57:22,458 --> 00:57:23,459
What's that?

960
00:57:24,627 --> 00:57:25,628
What's that?

961
00:57:30,533 --> 00:57:31,534
Darn it.

962
00:57:32,569 --> 00:57:35,104
Pre-Meeting with Client approved?

963
00:57:35,104 --> 00:57:36,105
What's this?

964
00:57:36,105 --> 00:57:37,373
The approval finally came through.

965
00:57:43,646 --> 00:57:47,016
All right, let's get our Meeting started,
shall we?

966
00:57:52,121 --> 00:57:53,623
Okay. We got it.

967
00:57:55,058 --> 00:57:56,059
Found it.

968
00:57:56,693 --> 00:57:57,694
I've sent the evidence.

969
00:57:58,127 --> 00:57:59,495
Requesting approval
for an emergency Meeting.

970
00:58:00,196 --> 00:58:03,433
So what do we do now?
Their equipment looks pretty intense.

971
00:58:03,433 --> 00:58:05,034
What if it comes to a physical fight?

972
00:58:05,034 --> 00:58:06,102
You worry too much.

973
00:58:06,569 --> 00:58:07,570
What?

974
00:58:08,771 --> 00:58:10,907
Hey, hey!

975
00:58:10,940 --> 00:58:12,308
Hey!

976
00:58:12,308 --> 00:58:14,210
Mr. Kim is from
Army Special Forces.

977
00:58:15,311 --> 00:58:17,313
He's especially skilled
in close-quarters combat.

978
00:58:19,616 --> 00:58:21,317
Oh my goodness.

979
00:58:21,918 --> 00:58:24,320
And Ms. Yang's hobby is
all kinds of combat sports.

980
00:58:24,320 --> 00:58:26,456
Judo, Taekwondo, and kickboxing.

981
00:58:27,357 --> 00:58:28,825
- There's nothing she can't do.
- Hey.

982
00:58:35,365 --> 00:58:36,666
Goodness.

983
00:58:40,537 --> 00:58:42,572
You're big, but completely useless.

984
00:58:44,741 --> 00:58:45,942
Manager Yu.

985
00:58:46,709 --> 00:58:47,710
Manager Yu.

986
00:58:54,183 --> 00:58:56,219
Hands up, you son of a gun.

987
00:58:58,721 --> 00:58:59,722
Gosh.

988
00:59:01,724 --> 00:59:03,092
An old man like you...

989
00:59:04,594 --> 00:59:08,731
shouldn't be playing
with something this dangerous.

990
00:59:10,433 --> 00:59:12,502
Gosh, it's hot. Darn it.

991
00:59:12,502 --> 00:59:15,939
Shut up.
Get to the wall and put your hands up.

992
00:59:18,608 --> 00:59:19,909
Hurry.

993
00:59:25,248 --> 00:59:26,249
You guys too.

994
00:59:27,283 --> 00:59:28,284
Darn it.

995
00:59:29,519 --> 00:59:31,254
Hey, push them against the wall.

996
00:59:34,424 --> 00:59:35,558
Mr. Kim.

997
00:59:35,592 --> 00:59:38,294
- Hey, stomp him.
- Darn it.

998
00:59:41,397 --> 00:59:42,866
Hey, hey.

999
00:59:44,000 --> 00:59:46,169
Try not to hit them in the gut.

1000
00:59:46,202 --> 00:59:47,637
They're 300 million a head.

1001
00:59:47,670 --> 00:59:49,005
- Yes.
- Yes.

1002
00:59:55,211 --> 00:59:59,549
What if a wolf appeared
when Mom is in the woods?

1003
00:59:59,582 --> 01:00:01,551
The wolf would be scared of your mom
and run away.

1004
01:00:01,851 --> 01:00:03,553
Is Mom stronger than a wolf?

1005
01:00:04,220 --> 01:00:07,357
Of course. Your mom is way stronger.
Your mom is super strong.

1006
01:00:08,358 --> 01:00:10,793
Even on rough mountain trails,
your mom just...

1007
01:00:10,793 --> 01:00:12,662
climbs them with no problem.

1008
01:00:12,695 --> 01:00:15,431
And even when the snow is piled high,
like an excavator,

1009
01:00:15,465 --> 01:00:17,000
she just clears a path.

1010
01:00:17,834 --> 01:00:20,703
She's strong enough
to lift me up with ease.

1011
01:00:23,473 --> 01:00:24,974
And...

1012
01:00:27,644 --> 01:00:29,946
She's also very daring.

1013
01:00:35,451 --> 01:00:37,086
The mom that I know...

1014
01:00:37,487 --> 01:00:41,257
is tough and strong,
but never loses her dignity.

1015
01:00:42,125 --> 01:00:43,426
She's a wonderful person like that.

1016
01:00:45,395 --> 01:00:49,032
What the hell?
Why is it so noisy?

1017
01:00:56,639 --> 01:00:58,408
Manager Yu, you're awake.

1018
01:00:58,441 --> 01:00:59,943
Manager Yu.

1019
01:00:59,976 --> 01:01:02,912
Darn it, who are the bastards
making all that noise?

1020
01:01:02,912 --> 01:01:04,280
I can't even sleep...

1021
01:01:04,581 --> 01:01:06,282
What is this? Who did this?

1022
01:01:06,316 --> 01:01:07,650
Who tied me up like this? Darn it.

1023
01:01:08,151 --> 01:01:09,152
Was it you?

1024
01:01:09,152 --> 01:01:12,288
Seriously, who the hell is this wench?

1025
01:01:12,288 --> 01:01:14,991
Why do these annoying gnats
keep buzzing around?

1026
01:01:15,825 --> 01:01:18,228
What? "Gnats?" This crazy...

1027
01:01:21,464 --> 01:01:22,765
- Darn it.
- Are you okay, sir?

1028
01:01:24,567 --> 01:01:27,604
You said you could handle this alone.
Did you get old already?

1029
01:01:27,637 --> 01:01:29,906
Well, I have gotten older.

1030
01:01:29,906 --> 01:01:32,575
But I was trying to
handle it myself anyway.

1031
01:01:32,609 --> 01:01:34,944
Since it's your first outing in a while,
Manager Yu,

1032
01:01:34,978 --> 01:01:37,814
I wanted you to drink and sleep
as much as you wanted.

1033
01:01:37,847 --> 01:01:39,849
That's why I was handling it alone,
but suddenly,

1034
01:01:40,750 --> 01:01:42,919
an old man showed up with a gun.

1035
01:01:44,020 --> 01:01:45,355
- A gun?
- Yes.

1036
01:01:45,388 --> 01:01:46,456
He has a gun?

1037
01:01:48,224 --> 01:01:50,894
Go ahead
and clean this up, Manager Yu.

1038
01:01:50,894 --> 01:01:52,695
Move, you darn idiots.

1039
01:01:55,732 --> 01:01:56,933
Hey.

1040
01:01:57,934 --> 01:01:58,968
Get on your knees.

1041
01:01:59,569 --> 01:02:00,770
- On your knees.
- On your knees.

1042
01:02:01,237 --> 01:02:04,774
- On your knees, you wench.
- What's that buzzing? An old fly?

1043
01:02:06,676 --> 01:02:07,744
This wench.

1044
01:02:08,678 --> 01:02:10,380
You want a hole in your head?

1045
01:02:12,048 --> 01:02:14,584
A hole in my head? That's my line.

1046
01:02:16,953 --> 01:02:18,021
You little...

1047
01:02:18,655 --> 01:02:22,025
Don't... Don't move.
If you move, I'll shoot.

1048
01:02:22,892 --> 01:02:24,160
You can't shoot if I'm moving.

1049
01:02:25,428 --> 01:02:27,997
You...

1050
01:02:28,031 --> 01:02:29,999
Is... Is she crazy?

1051
01:02:30,667 --> 01:02:32,669
Shoot. I'm standing still.

1052
01:02:36,873 --> 01:02:39,542
Fine. Die, you wench!

1053
01:02:42,045 --> 01:02:43,646
Gosh, sir!

1054
01:02:44,948 --> 01:02:46,049
Sir.

1055
01:02:46,449 --> 01:02:47,550
You can't even pull the trigger?

1056
01:02:51,454 --> 01:02:52,622
I'm not going to shoot. I won't.

1057
01:02:53,423 --> 01:02:54,424
You won't?

1058
01:03:01,898 --> 01:03:04,701
Let's get her. Hey, kill that bitch.

1059
01:03:04,734 --> 01:03:06,336
It's been a while. Shall we?

1060
01:03:06,336 --> 01:03:08,304
Come at me all at once, you flies.

1061
01:03:08,304 --> 01:03:09,906
Hey, kill her.

1062
01:03:13,243 --> 01:03:14,410
It slipped.

1063
01:03:15,545 --> 01:03:16,546
I guess I'll go without it.

1064
01:03:16,946 --> 01:03:18,548
You wench.

1065
01:03:42,272 --> 01:03:43,640
Yu Bo Na's drunk habits are showing.

1066
01:03:46,910 --> 01:03:47,911
Bo Na...

1067
01:03:56,953 --> 01:03:58,154
Hey!

1068
01:03:59,255 --> 01:04:00,623
Why do you keep getting up?

1069
01:04:06,596 --> 01:04:07,597
(Durumi Sales Team Workshop)

1070
01:04:15,271 --> 01:04:17,674
As agile as a puma,

1071
01:04:17,707 --> 01:04:19,576
as courageous as a lion,

1072
01:04:19,609 --> 01:04:22,111
and as elegant as a swan.

1073
01:04:22,145 --> 01:04:23,446
Back then, Yu Bo Na...

1074
01:04:25,014 --> 01:04:26,583
...was so beautiful.

1075
01:04:32,956 --> 01:04:33,957
Hey!

1076
01:05:02,452 --> 01:05:03,486
On your knees, you bastard.

1077
01:05:09,692 --> 01:05:12,428
Gosh, Yu Bo Na's still got it.

1078
01:05:46,429 --> 01:05:49,399
(A Bona fide Killer)

1079
01:05:49,432 --> 01:05:52,502
Yul, I told you Mommy can't today
because she has to go to work, right?

1080
01:05:52,502 --> 01:05:53,536
I hate you, Mommy.

1081
01:05:53,570 --> 01:05:55,438
So that guy
is getting out of prison after all?

1082
01:05:55,438 --> 01:05:57,373
We should probably move up the timeline.

1083
01:05:57,373 --> 01:05:58,942
Before he goes back
to his old neighborhood.

1084
01:05:58,942 --> 01:06:00,577
That could get pretty messy.

1085
01:06:00,610 --> 01:06:02,679
He died the same day
he was released.

1086
01:06:02,679 --> 01:06:05,215
What if we go after
the incidents that are about to happen?

1087
01:06:05,215 --> 01:06:06,783
Sir, welcome.

1088
01:06:07,283 --> 01:06:08,851
Kingfisher's next target.

1089
01:06:08,851 --> 01:06:11,554
- Is this related to Kingfisher?
- Were you following me?

1090
01:06:12,522 --> 01:06:13,856
What's going on, Mr. Kim?

1091
01:06:13,890 --> 01:06:15,725
I'm Pyo Gyu Cheol, you bastards.

1092
01:06:16,726 --> 01:06:19,662
So Manager Yu is
in the most dangerous position...

1093
01:06:19,662 --> 01:06:21,331
and has the highest risk of being caught.

1094
01:06:25,034 --> 01:06:26,035
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
